==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|frightfull}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|frightful||afraid}}, from {{inh|en|ang|forhtful||fainthearted, timorous}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|fright|ful}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|frīt′fəl}}, {{IPA|/ˈfɹaɪtfəl/|lang=en}}
* {{hyph|fright|ful|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-frightful.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[full|Full]] of [[fright]], ''whether''
## [[afraid|Afraid]], [[frightened]].
##* '''c. 1250''', ''Genesis and Exodus'', line 3459:
##*: [[this|Ðis]] '''frigtful''' [[thus|ðus]] a-biden,<br>Quiles [[this|ðis]] daiȝes [[forth|for]] ben gliden.
## [[timid|Timid]], [[fearful]], [[easily]] [[frightened]].
##* {{quote-book|lang=en|author=[[w:William Browne (poet)|William Browne]]|year=1613|title=Britannia's Pastorals|passage=See how the '''frightful''' herds run from the wood.}}
# [[full|Full]] of [[something]] [[causing]] [[fright]], ''whether''
## [[genuinely|Genuinely]] [[horrific]], [[awful]], or [[alarming]].
## {{lb|en|hyperbolic}} [[unpleasant|Unpleasant]], [[dreadful]], [[awful]] (''also used as an intensifier'').
##* '''1990''', ''[[w:House of Cards (UK TV show)|House of Cards]]'', Season 1, Episode 1:
##*: ''Francis Urquhart:'' What a '''frightful''' little man. Where do they find them these days?<br>''Tim Stamper:'' God knows. If I had a dog like that, I'd shoot it.<br>''Francis Urquhart:'' Well, yes. Quite.

